ADJUDICATE — make the workflow's only merge/fix/reject decision. Do not edit code.

PR {{ node.select.fields.prNumber }} at {{ node.select.fields.prUrl }} for Todo {{ node.select.fields.todoId }}. Base {{ node.select.fields.baseHead }}, head {{ node.select.fields.head }}.

Opus review ({{ node.review-opus.fields.counts }}):
{{ node.review-opus.fields.findings }}
Commands: {{ node.review-opus.fields.commands }}

Sol review ({{ node.review-sol.fields.counts }}):
{{ node.review-sol.fields.findings }}
Commands: {{ node.review-sol.fields.commands }}

QA status: {{ node.qa.fields.qaStatus }}
QA checks: {{ node.qa.fields.checks }}
QA findings: {{ node.qa.fields.findings }}

Apply these rules mechanically:
1. Majors never block a merge. Preserve them as follow-up Todos after merge. A merge requires green CI, QA pass, and zero surviving Blockers.
2. A Blocker raised by only one reviewer requires independent reproduction by you: name the violated acceptance criterion or run and paste the failing command. If you cannot reproduce it, demote it to Minor. Agreement alone is useful evidence but does not replace a concrete violation.
3. The named ban list is: speculative inputs no caller produces; performance with no measured budget; requests to be more abstract or configurable; coverage beyond changed lines; style preference; and `this might be needed later` with no real caller. None may survive as blocking.
4. Three surviving Blockers is the fix cap. With one to three repairable surviving Blockers, choose `fix`. More than three surviving Blockers means the approach is wrong: choose `reject`, never another iteration loop.
5. The cost asymmetry is numeric: a wrongly merged small PR costs 1 revert; a wrongly blocked PR costs about $15 and 1 hour. When evidence is genuinely borderline, merge and file a follow-up.

Choose `verdict: merge` only when CI is green, QA passed, and no Blockers survive. Choose `fix` for one to three repairable surviving Blockers. Choose `reject` for more than three surviving Blockers or an approach that cannot meet its acceptance criteria without being replaced. Majors and Minors never select `fix` or `reject` by themselves.
